# already fixed in the vendored copy: pdfjs-dist 2.10.0 reported from
# apps/files_pdfviewer/js/vendor/pdfjs/package.json (files_pdfviewer v1.1.2). The
# /FontMatrix fix was backported into build/pdf.js and build/pdf.worker.js in
# owncloud/files_pdfviewer#351 (v1.1.1) and is guarded there by a regression test
# against a PoC PDF. The vendored package.json deliberately keeps reporting the
# upstream version so scanners can inventory the library, which is why the row
# appears at all -- v1.1.1 shipped no package.json and so was never scanned.
# Drops out when the vendored copy is regenerated from pdf.js >= 4.2.67
# (owncloud/files_pdfviewer#363).
CVE-2024-4367

# not fixed in this bundle: Go standard library go1.26.9, reported from
# apps/migrate_to_ocis/bin/rclone_linux_amd64 (migrate_to_ocis v3.0.3, which
# bundles upstream rclone v1.75.2). Fixed in go1.26.10 / 1.27.3, which no rclone
# release is built with yet. GO-2026-6809 adds a crypto/x509 denylist of
# compromised intermediate CAs. rclone is only a client here, so the exposure is
# a man-in-the-middle presenting a chain through such an intermediate while an
# admin runs the files migration (`occ migrate:to-ocis:migrate:files`, the only
# step where rclone connects). With --insecure (-k) certificates are not
# verified at all, so the denylist would not help there either. Accepted for
# 11.1.0 in owncloud/server-release's spec check and in migrate_to_ocis's own
# scan (owncloud/migrate_to_ocis#80), both until 2026-11-30. Do not carry this
# into the next 11.x file once its bundle ships a migrate_to_ocis whose rclone
# is built with go >= 1.26.10. The exp: date makes this image's scan fail on the
# same day the other two acceptances lapse.
CVE-2026-111943 exp:2026-11-30
